---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mail Automation & IMb Tracking | USPS Intelligent Mail"
  description="Understanding USPS Intelligent Mail barcodes (IMb), automation-compatible mail, and how mail automation reduces postage costs and improves delivery tracking."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Mail Automation & IMb Tracking"
    subtitle="How USPS Intelligent Mail barcodes reduce your postage costs and enable real-time delivery tracking."
    breadcrumbs={[
      { label: 'Resources', href: '/resources' },
      { label: 'Mail Automation' },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="py-14 lg:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="section-divider mb-6"></div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-6">
          What Is Mail Automation?
        </h2>
        <p class="text-navy-600/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Mail automation refers to the USPS processing system that reads, sorts, and routes mail using barcodes and machine-readable addresses. Automation-compatible mail moves through the postal network faster and at lower cost because it requires less manual handling. For businesses sending bulk mail, automation compatibility is the single biggest factor in reducing postage rates.
        </p>
        <p class="text-navy-600/80 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Cornerstone prepares every mailing to meet USPS automation standards — from address formatting and barcode placement to tray labeling and container preparation. This ensures your mail qualifies for the lowest available postage rates.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-4">Intelligent Mail Barcode (IMb)</h3>
        <p class="text-navy-600/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          The Intelligent Mail barcode (IMb) is the USPS standard for tracking and routing mail through the postal network. It replaced the older POSTNET barcode and encodes significantly more data — including a unique tracking ID for every mailpiece. The IMb is required for automation pricing on First-Class and Marketing Mail.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-navy-50 rounded-xl p-6 mb-8">
          <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy-800 mb-3">What the IMb Encodes</h4>
          <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-navy-600/80">
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-crst-gold mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
              <div><strong>Barcode ID:</strong> Identifies the mail type and service (presort, automation, full-service)</div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-crst-gold mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
              <div><strong>Service Type ID:</strong> Specifies services requested (Address Change Service, return mail handling)</div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-crst-gold mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
              <div><strong>Mailer ID (MID):</strong> Identifies the sender — Cornerstone's MID or your company's MID</div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-crst-gold mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
              <div><strong>Serial Number:</strong> A unique number assigned to every individual mailpiece for tracking</div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-crst-gold mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
              <div><strong>Routing Code:</strong> The 11-digit delivery point ZIP+4 code that routes the piece to the correct carrier</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-4">Automation vs. Non-Automation Rates</h3>
        <p class="text-navy-600/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          The postage savings from automation compatibility are significant. Automation-rate mail typically costs 2–5 cents less per piece than non-automation mail. On a mailing of 10,000 pieces, that's $200–$500 in savings — just from proper barcode formatting and address processing.
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-crst-primary text-white">
                <th class="text-left p-3 rounded-tl-lg">Mail Type</th>
                <th class="text-right p-3">Automation Rate*</th>
                <th class="text-right p-3">Non-Automation Rate*</th>
                <th class="text-right p-3 rounded-tr-lg">Savings per Piece</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-800">Marketing Mail Letter (5-digit)</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.395</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.305</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-semibold">$0.058</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-gray-50">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-800">Marketing Mail Flat (5-digit)</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.558</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.672</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-semibold">$0.114</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-800">First-Class Letter (5-digit)</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.449</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.509</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-semibold">$0.060</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-gray-50">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-800">First-Class Flat (5-digit)</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.585</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.685</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-semibold">$0.100</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-2">*Rates approximate as of 2025. Actual rates depend on presort level, weight, and mail volume. Contact us for a current quote.</p>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-4">Full-Service IMb Benefits</h3>
        <p class="text-navy-600/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          USPS offers additional discounts for "Full-Service" IMb mailings. Full-Service requires submitting electronic documentation (eDoc) to USPS before the mailing enters the mail stream, and using unique IMb barcodes on every piece. In return, you receive:
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-5">
            <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Real-Time Delivery Tracking</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Every mailpiece is scanned as it moves through the USPS network. You can see when pieces hit processing facilities and when they're delivered — similar to package tracking but for letters and flats.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-5">
            <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Address Correction Notifications</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">When a recipient has moved, USPS provides electronic Change of Address (COA) notifications — allowing you to update your mailing list without paying for physical return mail.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-5">
            <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Postage Discounts</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Full-Service mailings receive a per-piece discount beyond standard automation rates. USPS incentivizes Full-Service because eDoc submissions help them plan mail processing more efficiently.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-5">
            <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Seamless Entry</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Full-Service mailings can be inducted at USPS facilities with less manual verification, speeding up the entry process and reducing delays.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-4">How Cornerstone Handles Automation</h3>
        <p class="text-navy-600/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          You don't need to worry about the technical details — we handle all automation requirements as part of our standard <a href="/services/mailing" class="text-crst-primary underline hover:text-crst-gold">mailing services</a>. Every mailing we produce includes CASS/DPV address validation, NCOA move-update processing, IMb barcode generation, Full-Service electronic documentation, presort optimization for maximum postal discounts, and tray/container labeling per USPS standards. Accurate address data is the foundation of automation — our <a href="/services/data-lists" class="text-crst-primary underline hover:text-crst-gold">data list services</a> ensure your mailing list is clean, current, and optimized for the deepest presort levels.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-crst-primary/5 border border-crst-primary/20 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-crst-primary mb-2">Want Delivery Tracking on Your Next Mailing?</h4>
          <p class="text-navy-600/80 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ask about IMb tracking and Full-Service mail when you request your next estimate. We'll show you exactly when your mail hits carrier routes.
          </p>
          <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary text-sm">Get a Free Estimate</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection />
</BaseLayout>
